# EtSelect Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtSelect` is a presentational select trigger component for the eToro design system. It provides a button-like interface to open select/selector modals with:

- **Single root component**: `<EtSelect>` with `type` prop (`'text'` or `'field'`)
- **Compound component API**: `EtSelect.Label`, `EtSelect.Value`, `EtSelect.LeadingContent`
- **Structured context**: `{ state, meta }` pattern for styling injection into subcomponents
- **Generic composition**: The dev composes whatever content they need (icons, flags, etc.)
- **Haptic feedback**: Enabled by default
- **Accessibility**: Uses React Native accessibility props (role, state, labels)

**Does NOT handle:**

- Select modal/dropdown logic (trigger only - parent manages modal state)
- Selection state management (parent controls displayed text)
- Validation or error states
- Specific icon types (clock, calendar, etc.) — the dev composes these themselves

## Entry Points & Contracts

### `EtSelect` (root component)

```ts
interface EtSelectProps {
  children: ReactNode;
  onPress: () => void;
  type?: 'text' | 'field'; // default: 'field'
  disabled?: boolean; // default: false (ignored for text type)
  readonly?: boolean; // default: false (field only) — see Readonly state below
  showChevron?: boolean; // default: true (field only) — readonly forces hidden unless disabled wins
  haptics?: boolean; // default: true
  width?: DimensionValue; // default: 335 (field type only)
  style?: StyleProp<ViewStyle>;
  testID?: string;
  accessibilityLabel?: string;
  accessibilityHint?: string;
}
```

### Type Behavior

#### `type="text"` — Inline text

- Renders semibold text with trailing chevron icon only (no leading icons)
- Always interactive (disabled prop is ignored)
- Flexible width, self-sizing
- `LeadingContent` is ignored in this type

#### `type="field"` — Bordered container

- Auto-switches between empty (placeholder) and filled appearance
- Filled state triggers when `EtSelect.Label` or `EtSelect.LeadingContent` is present
- Supports disabled state
- Fixed width (default 335px)

### Compound Subcomponents

| Subcomponent              | Purpose                             | Used in                   |
| ------------------------- | ----------------------------------- | ------------------------- |
| `EtSelect.Label`          | Label text above value              | Field type (filled state) |
| `EtSelect.Value`          | Value/placeholder text              | Both types                |
| `EtSelect.LeadingContent` | Content before value (icon or flag) | Field type only           |

## Architecture

### Composition Philosophy

This component is **generic** — it does NOT include built-in icons for specific use cases (clock, calendar, country, etc.). Instead, the developer composes whatever content they need via compound children. This means:

- No `EtSelectType` enum for icon selection
- No built-in icon rendering logic
- The UI kit stays lean; the dev builds the input as needed

### File Structure

```text
select/
├── api/
│   ├── index.ts          # Public API exports
│   └── types.ts          # EtSelectProps, subcomponent props, EtSelectType
├── context/
│   ├── index.ts
│   └── select-context.tsx # Context with { state, meta } interface
├── hooks/
│   ├── index.ts
│   ├── use-select-config.ts    # Configuration: colors, sizes, borders
│   └── use-select-children.ts  # Children processing: extract compound children
├── subcomponents/
│   ├── index.ts
│   ├── select-label.tsx          # EtSelect.Label (body-secondary-medium)
│   ├── select-value.tsx          # EtSelect.Value (heading-large or heading-compact)
│   └── select-leading-content.tsx # EtSelect.LeadingContent (passthrough)
├── et-select.tsx          # Root component + Object.assign for compound API
├── et-select.test.tsx     # Tests
├── index.ts               # Public exports
└── AGENTS.mdc              # This file
```

### Data Flow

1. Consumer renders `<EtSelect type="text"|"field" ...>` with compound children
2. `EtSelectBase` (root component):
   a. `useSelectChildren` → extracts compound children by displayName
   b. Detects `hasValue` (field only) based on Label/LeadingContent presence
   c. `useSelectConfig` → computes `{ state, meta }` context + border/bg colors
   d. Wraps children in `SelectContext.Provider`
   e. Renders layout based on `type` prop
3. Subcomponents → consume `{ state, meta }` context for auto-styling

### Context Interface

```ts
interface SelectContextValue {
  state: {
    type: 'text' | 'field';
    disabled: boolean;
    readonly: boolean;
  };
  meta: {
    textColor: string;
    labelColor: string;
    iconColor: string;
    iconSize: number;
  };
}
```

## Usage Patterns

### Text Type

```tsx
<EtSelect type="text" onPress={handlePress}>
  <EtSelect.Value>Select</EtSelect.Value>
</EtSelect>

// String shorthand
<EtSelect type="text" onPress={handlePress}>Select</EtSelect>
```

> **Note:** Text type renders only the value text + chevron. `LeadingContent` is ignored.

### Field Type

```tsx
// Empty placeholder
<EtSelect type="field" onPress={handlePress}>
  <EtSelect.Value>Select</EtSelect.Value>
</EtSelect>

// With value (auto-filled appearance via Label)
<EtSelect type="field" onPress={handlePress}>
  <EtSelect.Label>Time</EtSelect.Label>
  <EtSelect.Value>10:15 AM</EtSelect.Value>
</EtSelect>

// With country flag (dev composes the flag)
<EtSelect type="field" onPress={handlePress}>
  <EtSelect.Label>Country of residence</EtSelect.Label>
  <EtSelect.LeadingContent>
    <EtCountryFlag isoCode="GB" size={20} />
  </EtSelect.LeadingContent>
  <EtSelect.Value>United Kingdom</EtSelect.Value>
</EtSelect>

// Disabled
<EtSelect type="field" onPress={handlePress} disabled>
  <EtSelect.Label>Country</EtSelect.Label>
  <EtSelect.Value>United Kingdom</EtSelect.Value>
</EtSelect>

// Readonly (locked value, normal colors, no chevron) — pair with i18n'd accessibilityHint
<EtSelect
  type="field"
  onPress={handlePress}
  readonly
  accessibilityHint={t('payee.country_locked_hint')}
>
  <EtSelect.Label>Account country</EtSelect.Label>
  <EtSelect.LeadingContent>
    <EtCountryFlag isoCode="DK" size={20} />
  </EtSelect.LeadingContent>
  <EtSelect.Value>Denmark</EtSelect.Value>
</EtSelect>

// Field with no chevron (rare — for custom triggers without affordance)
<EtSelect type="field" onPress={handlePress} showChevron={false}>
  <EtSelect.Value>Custom</EtSelect.Value>
</EtSelect>
```

### Readonly state (field only)

`readonly` provides a third interaction state alongside enabled/disabled, for values that are
**locked but not unavailable** (e.g. DKK accounts where country is fixed to Denmark).

| Slot                   | Enabled                | Readonly                  | Disabled         | Disabled + Readonly         |
| ---------------------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------- | ---------------- | --------------------------- |
| Value text (filled)    | `carbon900`            | `carbon900`               | `carbon300`      | `carbon300`                 |
| Value text (empty)     | `carbon500`            | `carbon500`               | `carbon300`      | `carbon300`                 |
| Label                  | `carbon500`            | `carbon500`               | `carbon300`      | `carbon300`                 |
| Chevron icon           | `carbon500`            | _(hidden)_                | `carbon300`      | `carbon300` (visible)       |
| Pressable              | enabled                | enabled (handler no-ops)  | `disabled={true}`| `disabled={true}`           |
| Haptics                | yes                    | no                        | no               | no                          |
| `accessibilityState.disabled` | `false`         | `false`                   | `true`           | `true`                      |

**Precedence (D5):** when both `disabled` and `readonly` are set, **`disabled` wins** — including
chevron visibility. This keeps a globally-disabled form visually uniform across all fields.

**Implementation note (D1):** `Pressable.disabled` is driven by `isDisabled`, never by `isReadonly`.
Readonly relies on `handlePress` no-op'ing internally so platform a11y semantics
(`accessibilityState.disabled = false`) stay honest. Setting `Pressable.disabled=true` would force
VoiceOver / TalkBack to announce "disabled" regardless of the explicit accessibilityState override.

### `showChevron` history

Originally introduced in commit `632eccfa48` (EtPicker → EtSelect rename) with default `true`.
**Removed** in commit `ddd0f29a4f` (Feb 2026) for "API simplicity / consistent visual appearance,"
then **re-introduced** for PAH-384 to support the readonly state. Default remains `true` for
backward compatibility. Do not remove without auditing consumers in send-payment-payee, KYC, and
W8BEN forms — they may rely on `readonly` (which is implemented as a chevron-hide path).

## Anti-patterns

### ❌ Using dot notation on root component

```tsx
// BAD - root component is <EtSelect>, not <EtSelect.Field>
<EtSelect.Field onPress={handlePress}>...</EtSelect.Field>
```

**Fix:** Use the `type` prop:

```tsx
<EtSelect type="field" onPress={handlePress}>
  ...
</EtSelect>
```

### ❌ Using for form input

```tsx
// BAD - EtSelect is not an input field
<EtSelect type="field" onPress={() => {}}>
  <EtSelect.Value>{userInput}</EtSelect.Value>
</EtSelect>
```

**Fix:** Use `EtInput` for text input. `EtSelect` is only for triggering selects/modals.

### ❌ Using Label in text type

```tsx
// BAD - Label is only used in field type's filled state
<EtSelect type="text" onPress={handlePress}>
  <EtSelect.Label>Category</EtSelect.Label>
  <EtSelect.Value>All</EtSelect.Value>
</EtSelect>
```

**Fix:** `Label` is only used in field type. For text type, use just `Value`.

### ❌ Hardcoding English a11y strings for readonly state

```tsx
// BAD - accessibilityValue is not part of EtSelectProps (won't compile).
// Even if it were, hardcoded English a11y text breaks non-EN locales.
<EtSelect type="field" onPress={...} readonly accessibilityValue={{ text: 'read-only' }}>
```

**Fix:** `EtSelect` deliberately omits `accessibilityValue` from its API to prevent hardcoded
strings at the component level. Consumers pass an i18n'd `accessibilityHint` describing the
locked state, so non-English locales hear the right string:

```tsx
<EtSelect
  type="field"
  onPress={...}
  readonly
  accessibilityHint={t('send_payment.payee.field.country_locked_hint')}
>
```

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal Dependencies

- `useEtoroTheme` (via `useSelectConfig`) - provides theme colors
- `EtText` - text rendering in subcomponents and fallback
- `EtoroIcon` - chevron-down trailing icon
- `SelectContext` - shares `{ state, meta }` with compound subcomponents

### External Dependencies

- `expo-haptics` - haptic feedback on press
- `react-native` - `Pressable`, `View`, `StyleSheet`

### Design System Integration

Colors map to V2 carbon tokens via `useEtoroTheme().colors`. Slot → token:

| Slot | V2 token |
| --- | --- |
| Text type value / icon (idle) | `carbon900` |
| Field type placeholder + chevron (idle, empty) | `carbon500` |
| Field type filled value | `carbon900` |
| Field type label (filled) + chevron (filled) | `carbon500` |
| All disabled (text / label / icon) | `carbon300` |
| Field background overlay | `${carbon900}0D` (carbon900 at ~5% opacity) |

- **Typography**:
  - Text type: `heading-large` (22px, semibold, lh 28, ls -0.25)
  - Field: `heading-compact` (18px, medium, lh 24)
  - Field (filled) label: `body-secondary-medium` (14px, medium, lh 20)
- **Icons**: 24px for text type, 20px for field (chevron-down only)
- **Layout**:
  - Text: flexible width, 28px min-height, gap 4px (X1)
  - Field (empty): 335px default width, 68px height, 12px radius, borderless
  - Field (filled): 335px default width, 68px height, 8px radius, borderless
- **Spacing**: X1 (4), X2 (8), X3 (12), X5 (20), X7 (28), X17 (68)

### Behavior deltas (V1 → V2)

The strict-Figma migration to V2 (`45107:26668`) introduced three intentional visual changes beyond the token swap:

1. **Field background** flips from a solid surface (`bgNeutralPrimary` — white in light, near-black in dark) to a translucent `carbon900` overlay at ~5% (`#1B1E210D`), so the field now blends into whatever surface it sits on.
2. **1px border removed entirely.** The previous reverse-polarity ternary (`disabled` stronger than `enabled`) is gone — `borderWidth: 0` on both `fieldContainer` and `filledContainer`. Figma "Field" state is borderless.
3. **`CONTENT_OPACITY = 0.8` removed.** The inner row no longer dims to 80%; placeholder + chevron render at full opacity, with `carbon500` providing the muted tone via the token instead of a runtime opacity multiplier.

